    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12578" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dĕcŭrĭālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		decuria, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			decuria</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leges,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 11, 13, 2</span></i>
			; hence <i>subst., a member of a decuria</i>
			(mostly post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">numerus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Anim. 37</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">DECVRIALIVM GERVLORVM DISPENSATOR,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 874</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">976</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2252</span></i>; 3216 al.; Fragm. Vat.
			§ 142.</div>
